              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "живой (zhivóy) — \"alive, lively\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "живой (zhivóy) from Proto-Slavic živŭ — inherited. Vasmer lists Lithuanian gývas, Sanskrit jīvá-, Latin vīvus and Gothic qius, all \"alive\": English quick, in its old sense \"alive\", is a cousin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
